Sun Nov 15 10:02:45 UTC 2026 - Johannes Kastl <opensuse_buildservice@ojkastl.de>

- Update to version 0.6.2:
  This release adds container-level CFS CPU throttling visibility
  and an at-a-glance Cluster Health Score percentage in the
  overview header.
  * Features
    - CFS CPU Throttling (#167):
      - Added container_cpu_cfs_throttled_seconds_total,
        container_cpu_cfs_throttled_periods_total, and
        container_cpu_cfs_periods_total to the Prometheus metric
        allowlist.
      - Computed per-container and pod-level CFS CPU throttling
        percentages (preferring throttled/total period ratios with
        a throttled-seconds rate fallback).
      - Added a sortable THROTTLE column (key h) to the Overview
        Pods table (toggleable via the C column selector and
        persisted in ~/.ktop/config.yaml) and the Pod Detail
        Containers table, plus a CFS: indicator in the Pod Detail
        Info header.
    - Cluster Health Score (#170):
      - Added a composite 0–100 cluster health score calculated
        from node readiness, failed/OOM pods, PSI saturation stalls
        (>20%), node pressure conditions, and metrics availability.
      - Rendered color-coded Health: <score>% in the Cluster
        Summary header (green ≥90%, yellow ≥70%, orange ≥50%, red
        <50%).

